1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,528
This is the moment every vibe coder lives for.

2
00:00:03,728 --> 00:00:09,631
You asked AI to build it. And it did. All of it.

3
00:00:09,832 --> 00:00:12,711
And then, three seconds later...

4
00:00:12,912 --> 00:00:15,096
...it all falls apart.

5
00:00:15,295 --> 00:00:19,135
Three days ago, Vee discovered something magical.

6
00:00:19,335 --> 00:00:26,775
You type what you want. AI builds it. Five minutes. Done.

7
00:00:26,975 --> 00:00:36,840
A to-do app. Done. A database. Done. A login page. Done.

8
00:00:37,039 --> 00:00:39,655
She thought she could build anything.

9
00:00:39,856 --> 00:00:43,167
But there was someone who'd seen this story before.

10
00:00:43,368 --> 00:00:45,456
She couldn't answer.

11
00:00:45,655 --> 00:00:47,840
Here's an empty lot.

12
00:00:48,039 --> 00:00:50,560
You want to build something here.

13
00:00:50,759 --> 00:01:02,039
With a blueprint, you start with the foundation. Then the frame. Then the walls. There's an order. Each piece knows where it goes.

14
00:01:02,240 --> 00:01:04,376
Without a blueprint?

15
00:01:04,575 --> 00:01:10,912
You just... stack. And it goes up. It actually goes up.

16
00:01:11,111 --> 00:01:14,207
For a while, it looks like it's working.

17
00:01:14,408 --> 00:01:15,896
Then...

18
00:01:16,096 --> 00:01:24,207
A spec is a blueprint. It's not a hundred-page document. It's one sentence: "What am I building?"

19
00:01:24,408 --> 00:01:27,647
You don't need to know every detail upfront.

20
00:01:27,847 --> 00:01:35,311
Start with a skateboard. Four wheels. It rolls. That's enough.

21
00:01:35,512 --> 00:01:40,959
You can always make it bigger later. But you have to know what "it" is first.

22
00:01:41,159 --> 00:01:45,408
That one line? That's where a spec starts.

23
00:01:45,608 --> 00:01:49,927
Back in the present. Everything still broken.

24
00:01:50,128 --> 00:01:55,072
And then she did something unusual. She stopped coding.

25
00:01:55,272 --> 00:02:01,703
She started writing. Not code. Just... what was bothering her.

26
00:02:01,903 --> 00:02:06,415
And there it was. The question she'd been avoiding.

27
00:02:06,615 --> 00:02:15,183
Not features. Not tools. The reason. The one sentence that explains everything.

28
00:02:15,383 --> 00:02:20,304
The same errors. But now, one line makes sense.

29
00:02:20,503 --> 00:02:23,000
Everything is still broken.

30
00:02:23,199 --> 00:02:25,912
But now she knows what to fix.

31
00:02:26,111 --> 00:02:28,919
...at least, she thinks she does.

